WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.071
Priya owns a bakery with twenty workers and is collecting quotes.

00:00:04.071 --> 00:00:07.772
The first carrier is a stock insurer, owned by shareholders

00:00:07.772 --> 00:00:11.103
who expect a profit; its policies are usually nonparticipating.

00:00:11.103 --> 00:00:15.174
The second is a mutual insurer, owned by its policyholders, who

00:00:15.174 --> 00:00:19.245
may receive dividends when results are good; those policies are participating.

00:00:19.245 --> 00:00:22.946
A fraternal benefit society sells only to its members through

00:00:22.946 --> 00:00:26.277
a lodge system and operates on a nonprofit basis.

00:00:26.277 --> 00:00:31.089
A large employer might instead self-insure, paying its own claims from company funds

00:00:31.089 --> 00:00:35.900
and hiring an administrator to process them, often with stop-loss protection behind it.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.480
Private insurers sell voluntary coverage for a premium.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.060
Government programs fill gaps the private market leaves.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:47.535
Medicare covers people 65 and older and certain disabled people.

00:00:47.535 --> 00:00:50.220
Medicaid serves people with limited income.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.248
Social Security pays disability income after a strict test.

00:00:54.248 --> 00:00:59.618
Workers compensation covers job injuries under state law, and in Maryland employers

00:00:59.618 --> 00:01:04.988
buy that coverage from private insurers or the Chesapeake Employers’ Insurance Company.

00:01:04.988 --> 00:01:06.778
TRICARE serves military families.

00:01:06.778 --> 00:01:13.042
When a question mixes programs and policies, decide first whether the payer is a

00:01:13.042 --> 00:01:18.860
private company accepting premium or a government program funded by taxes and mandates.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:24.130
An admitted, or authorized, insurer holds a certificate of authority from

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:28.922
the Maryland Insurance Administration and may sell in the state.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:32.755
A nonadmitted insurer does not, and its policies

00:01:32.755 --> 00:01:36.108
lack the protection of Maryland’s guaranty corporation.

00:01:36.108 --> 00:01:38.983
Separately, every insurer has a home.

00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:42.337
A domestic insurer is incorporated in Maryland.

00:01:42.337 --> 00:01:47.607
A foreign insurer is incorporated in another state, such as Delaware.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:51.440
An alien insurer is incorporated in another country.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.273
Foreign does not mean overseas on the exam.

00:01:55.273 --> 00:01:59.106
A Pennsylvania company selling in Baltimore is foreign

00:01:59.106 --> 00:02:02.460
and, if it holds a certificate, admitted.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:08.321
Before Priya trusts a carrier with her staff’s claims, Theo checks its financial strength.

00:02:08.321 --> 00:02:10.832
Independent rating services such as A.M.

00:02:10.832 --> 00:02:14.181
Best, Standard and Poor’s, Moody’s and Fitch grade

00:02:14.181 --> 00:02:17.112
insurers on their ability to pay claims.

00:02:17.112 --> 00:02:22.972
Operating results, including loss ratios and surplus, show whether the company is pricing soundly.

00:02:22.972 --> 00:02:27.996
Ratings are opinions, not guarantees, and a producer must never misrepresent them.

00:02:27.996 --> 00:02:32.601
Maryland regulators also monitor solvency through required financial statements and examinations.

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:35.950
A strong rating lowers the chance that the

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.880
guaranty corporation ever has to step in.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.482
Insurers distribute coverage in several ways.

00:02:41.482 --> 00:02:46.687
A career or captive agency system uses producers who represent one insurer.

00:02:46.687 --> 00:02:50.156
An independent agency system uses producers who place

00:02:50.156 --> 00:02:53.626
business with several insurers and own their expirations.

00:02:53.626 --> 00:02:57.963
Brokers represent the buyer in placing coverage, although in Maryland

00:02:57.963 --> 00:03:01.866
both agents and brokers hold the same producer license.

00:03:01.866 --> 00:03:06.637
Direct response sells by mail, phone or internet with no producer.

00:03:06.637 --> 00:03:10.973
Managing general agents administer business for insurers in a territory.

00:03:10.973 --> 00:03:14.009
Banks and employers also serve as channels.

00:03:14.009 --> 00:03:18.780
The system affects who the producer represents and how commissions flow.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:23.965
Maryland law recognizes three kinds of organizations that deliver health benefits.

00:03:23.965 --> 00:03:28.679
An insurer, defined broadly in the Insurance Article, is a

00:03:28.679 --> 00:03:33.393
person engaged as a principal in the business of insurance.

00:03:33.393 --> 00:03:39.521
A nonprofit health service plan is organized under Title 14 to provide health

00:03:39.521 --> 00:03:45.178
services on a prepaid or indemnity basis to subscribers, not for profit.

00:03:45.178 --> 00:03:50.834
A health maintenance organization combines financing and delivery of care, is authorized

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:56.491
under the Health-General Article and must hold a certificate of authority from

00:03:56.491 --> 00:04:01.676
the Insurance Commissioner, with the Maryland Department of Health overseeing quality.

00:04:01.676 --> 00:04:06.390
All three must obey Maryland’s mandated benefits and consumer protections.
